<title>CHINA: China completes construction on Huizhou wharf.</title>
<headline>China completes construction on Huizhou wharf.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 1.5 billion yuan ($180 million) wharf in southern China has begun operation after two years' construction, the Economic Information Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The project in Huizhou port in China's southern province of Guangdong included deepwater berths, a 10 km sea pipeline and a 1,632 km of land oil pipelines, the newspaper said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
